# The wolf: a creature of the Mists (WLD-56; Sitting E §§ 6–7). Ruled by Darko 2026-10-15 12:09 (D4).
# Its aggression is display only: no nerve, no harm (tools/creature-kind.mjs refuses either).
kind: wolf
name: a grey wolf
voice: a lean grey wolf at the edge of the fog, its eyes catching what light there is
about: a wolf out of the Mists; it watches, warns and paces, and goes back when it has had enough
what: >
  A wolf that came out of the Mists with the season. It is wary of the town and curious about it in
  equal measure, and it shows its teeth more than it means them. Come too close and it warns you;
  frighten it and it is gone back into the grey.
ring_m: 80
# what it likes, read by Jev with judgment (POS-672, ruled 2026-10-16 18:06; the words are a draft for Darko)
tastes: Meat and bones, and anything that smells of the town's kitchens; it sniffs at sweets and seldom takes them.
moods:
  fear: 0..3 = 1 | unbothered | wary | uneasy | ready to bolt
  curiosity: 0..3 = 1 | indifferent | watchful | interested | fixed on you
  hunger: 0..3 = 2 | fed | peckish | hungry | starving

reaction watch "it stands still and watches": when true says At the edge of the Mists a grey wolf stands perfectly still, watching {actor}.
reaction snarl "it bares its teeth, a warning only": when act.approaching and act.distance_m < 40 says The wolf's lip curls back. It snarls at {actor}, low and steady.
reaction stalk "it paces along the mist-line with you": when act.verb == "walk" says The wolf paces along the edge of the Mists, keeping level with {actor}, never closer.
reaction howl "it throws back its head and howls": when self.hunger >= 2 says The wolf throws back its head and howls. Deep in the Mists, something answers.
reaction slink "it slinks back a step into the fog": when self.fear >= 2 does self.fear -1 says The wolf slinks back a step into the fog, its eyes still on {actor}.
reaction flee "it turns and is gone": when self.fear >= 3 does flee says The wolf wheels and is gone, a grey shape folding back into the grey.

# Its afforded actions' reactions (POS-672; the lines approved by Darko 2026-10-20 22:35): a
# resident aims watch, approach, shoo, call or offer at it, and one of these, or one above, is the reply.
reaction hold "it holds your eye": when act.verb == "watch" says The wolf holds {actor}'s eye, unblinking, until the fog moves between you.
reaction give "it gives ground, slowly": when act.verb == "approach" does self.fear +1 says The wolf gives ground, slowly, never taking its eyes off {actor}.
reaction bristle "its hackles rise": when act.verb == "shoo" does self.fear +1 says The wolf's hackles rise; it gives {actor} one step and no more.
reaction answer "it answers with a long howl": when act.verb == "call" says The wolf lifts its head and answers {actor}'s call with a long howl.
reaction ears "its ears swivel to you": when act.verb == "call" says The wolf's ears swivel toward {actor}; it does not move.
reaction accept "it takes it": when act.verb == "offer" and self.fear <= 2 does self.hunger -1 says The wolf waits until {actor} steps back, then takes the {offered} in one snap.
reaction sniff "it sniffs and turns away": when act.verb == "offer" says The wolf sniffs at the {offered} in {actor}'s hand, then turns its head away.
